Mel-Band RoFormer

model.py is taken from ZFTurbo's Music-Source-Separation-Training,
models/bs_roformer/mel_band_roformer.py and models/bs_roformer/attend.py
(https://github.com/ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training, MIT, see
LICENSE in this directory), itself derived from lucidrains' BS-RoFormer (MIT).
It loads the "Kim" vocals checkpoint (KimberleyJSN/melbandroformer, MIT).

Changes, to keep the worker small and the module names equal to the
checkpoint's keys (it loads with strict=True):

- inference only: the training loss, multi-stem heads, linear attention, PoPE,
  checkpointing, flash-attention backend selection and beartype are removed;
- the constructor takes a MelBandRoformerConfig dataclass
  (note_detector/separation_config.py) instead of keyword arguments;
- the mel filter bank comes from note_detector/mel_filters.py instead of
  librosa;
- attention is torch's scaled_dot_product_attention;
- the forward pass is split into helper methods.

The weights are not part of this repository; they are downloaded at image
build time and verified by sha256 (see apps/note-detector/Dockerfile).
